          <m>
            \begin{align*}
              \frac{3x}{3} &= \frac{9}{3} \\
              x &= 3
            \end{align*}
          </m>
          Therefore, the solution to the equation <m>3x + 2 = 11</m> is <m>x = 3</m>.
